// mecatl driver API: the remote session-store protocol.
//
// SessionStoreService is the wire seam behind the harness's `port.SessionStore`
// (engine/port/store.go): an operator-run driver process persists session
// snapshots on behalf of the harness, in place of the in-process stores
// (memstore, jsonlstore). The driver sits at the SAME trust tier as an
// on-disk store directory — operator-configured infrastructure, not a
// model-facing surface.
//
// The snapshot payload is OPAQUE to the driver: it is exactly the
// engine/adapter/sessnap encoding, identified by the envelope's `format` tag
// ("sessnap-json/1" today; see internal/adapter/grpcdriver.SnapshotFormat).
// The driver stores and returns the envelope VERBATIM and never decodes it —
// snapshot schema evolution lives in sessnap (additive JSON), while format
// identification lives in this envelope. The harness rejects an unknown
// `format` on Load with an infrastructure error (never not-found).
//
// Driver contract (mirrors the in-process stores):
//   - Load of an unknown session id MUST return NOT_FOUND.
//   - Save overwrites: Load returns the most recent snapshot saved under the id.
//
